        "heading_dh6Hhg": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "The Affordable Care Act (ACA)",
            "heading_size": "h3",
            "heading_h1": false
          }
        },
        "text_Hq4Qc8": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Under the Affordable Care Act (ACA), most health insurance plans are required to cover breastfeeding support, counseling, and <a href=\"https://www.ameda.com/pages/insurance\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">free or reduced-cost breast pumps</span></a> for the duration of breastfeeding. This includes both Marketplace plans and other health insurance plans, although some grandfathered plans may not offer the same coverage. Knowing that these services are often covered by your healthcare provider can significantly reduce out-of-pocket costs and make it easier to access high-quality Lactation Support. Learn more about getting a <a href=\"https://www.ameda.com/pages/insurance\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">breast pump through insurance</span></a> <a href=\"https://www.ameda.com/pages/insurance\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">here</span></a>. </p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        }
      },
