    "faq_KxDHU9": {
      "type": "faq",
      "blocks": {
        "question_EaUFkH": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "What if My Plan Is Grandfathered?",
            "text": "<p>If your insurance plan does not cover lactation services under the ACA, contact The Nest or The Lactation Network to discuss self-pay options. Some providers offer discounted rates or sliding scale fees for parents paying out of pocket.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_FewbJQ": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "What Should I Expect During a Lactation Consultation?",
            "text": "<p>During a typical consultation, a lactation consultant will assess your baby’s latch, answer questions about milk supply, and provide guidance on pumping or supplementing if needed. They’ll also help you feel more confident about handling common breastfeeding concerns at home.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_tyjcnM": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "What Equipment Is Covered Under the ACA?",
            "text": "<p>Many insurance plans cover the cost of breast pumps and related breastfeeding supplies. Ameda’s wide range of breastfeeding products is also available for parents seeking high-quality pumps and accessories. Learn more about how to get a <a href=\"https://www.ameda.com/pages/insurance\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">FREE breast pump through insurance</span></a> <a href=\"https://www.ameda.com/pages/insurance\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">here</span></a>. </p>"
          }
        }
      },
